//customized locators - in a complex websites -> using one locator is not enough for finding the web element -> in that case, we use to specify the targeted element by using customized locators 
                        -> uses tag and attribute values to locate a element
// CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) selector: (adding tags is optional -> we can use css selector for id as #id)
1. tag id -> html_tag#id
2. tag name -> html_tag.class_name
3. tag attribute -> tag[attribute = value] (values can be enclosed within '' or "" quotes) [[so important -> in java text which is enclosed within "" cannot be hold value with "", so we need to mention the value in ("tagname[attribute ='value']") or by using ("tagname[attribute =\"value\"]")  ]]
4. tag class attribute -> tag.class_name[attribute = value] (values can be enclosed within '' or "" quotes)
   -> it will be used if incase we have two fields
    username - _____________     <input class = "abcd" name = "123">
    password - _____________     <input class = "abcd" name = "567">
in the above two input fields the class name is same and other locator primary like id, class, linkText, partialLinkText are not same or not available, then we can use this cssSelector method to locate the web element
by (By.cssSelector("input.abcd[name='123']")); - username field or (By.cssSelector("input.abcd[name=\"567\"]")); - password field

